A('Z0770', 'nothing', 'Proof: the swap (u,v)↦(v,u) has fixed points u=v with n=u(tu−2), which for prime n forces u∈{1,n} and then t=n+2 ≡3 (4) or t=3/n, neither ≡0 (4) with t≥4; so for every odd prime the swap is fixed-point-free and R(p) is even. Numerically R(n) ≡ #diagonal words (mod 2) for all n≤1e5, and no diagonal word exists at primes ≡1 (4) ≤2e5.',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_census1e8.py', D + 'census1e8_results.json'], 'A second involution on the off-diagonal words was not sought.', 'Look for a second involution on the (u<v) words with computable fixed points.')
