A('Z0787', 'nothing', 'Premise false: the ES cubic 4xyz = p(xy+yz+zx)w has three A1 nodes at the coordinate points (Gröbner basis; quadratic part discriminant p² ≠ 0); its minimal resolution is a weak del Pezzo surface of degree 3 with Pic ≅ I^{1,6}, in which no nonzero class has D²=0 and K·D=0 (Cauchy–Schwarz). So there is no genus-one fibration to compute ranks on; the pencil x=y=0 splits into a line and a conic.',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_cubic_singular.py', 'GEOMETRY_ES.md', 'GLOBAL_FANO.md'], 'Rank computations (no object).', 'Replace by a conic-bundle analysis if a Selmer-type question is wanted.')
A('Z0797', 'nothing', 'All 135 reduced positive ternary forms with det ≤12 (66 non-constant r_Q) were tested against the residual U on 1114 primes ≡1 (4) ≤6000: best |ρ| = 0.68 (form (1,2,6,…), det 11), below the residual L(1,χ_p) baseline 0.75, so no form beats the L-value proxy. Several det-7 forms track L(1,χ_p) better (ρ=−0.86) than U (ρ=0.61).',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_forms2.py', D + 'forms2_results.json'], 'Forms with det >12 not enumerated.', 'Extend to det ≤40 with a numpy lattice counter.')
A('Z0802', 'nothing', 'R-zeros ≤1e8 among primes ≡1 (4): 409, 577, 5569, 9601, 23929, 83449, 102001, 329617, 712321, 1134241, 1724209, 1726201, and 14 in total (≤1e8). Quantile of L(1,χ_p) among same-size primes: 11 of the 12 zeros ≤3e6 are above 0.85 (least QNR 5–23). Logistic regression on 108 283 primes (12 events): logL1 coefficient 4.16 (SE 1.0), in-sample AUC 0.93.',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_logit.py', 'scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_cmin.py', D + 'logit_results.json'], 'Zeros in (3e6, 1e8] not given quantiles.', 'Compute L(1,χ_p) for the 2 zeros above 3e6 and place them in the table.')
