A('Z0836', 'interesting', 'Per-numerator count law: out-of-sample (fit on primes ≤3·10⁴, test on (3·10⁴,10⁵]) the predicted lowest log(1+U_m) identifies the m/p failures with median AUC 0.74 over the 25 numerators with test failures (in-sample 0.93 drops to 0.74).',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_fix_d.py', D + 'fix_d_results.json', D + 'auc_results.json'], 'Per-m Euler weights (a different count model per m) not fitted.', 'Compare the out-of-sample AUC with a model using Legendre weights per numerator.')
A('Z0839', 'nothing', 'Partial, scope stated: the (★)-slot image is computed exactly (explicit map (x,y,z)=(Cuv, pCv, pCu) for t=4C): it contains 13% of the solutions for p≡1 (4) and 5% for p≡3 (4) (40% and 19% of the Type-II solutions), and no Type-I solution (both formulas give p|y and p|z). The maps for the other four slots (4|u, 4|tu−1, 4|tv−1, 4|v) are not in the repository and were not derived, so the five-slice fraction is not complete.',
  ['scripts/z52d_p2_TO3_fiveslot.py', 'LOWERTAIL_DEEP_FABLE.md §1.1', D + 'fiveslot_results.json'], 'Maps for the four non-(★) slots (word → 4/p solution); needed for the Type-I solutions.', 'Derive the four remaining slot maps from the Farey pentagon (LOWER_TAIL_ASTRA) and rerun the fraction to 10⁴.')
